course: dictionary
lesson: 6171
title: Many meanings of minister
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Minister» can mean a government leader, a church leader, or a person who looks after someone. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning to use.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about. «The cabinet is the top team of ministers; a minister is in charge of one area, like health or education.» The clues are cabinet, health and education, so this is the government meaning.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. In church, a minister leads the services, so «the minister led the service» makes sense. «To minister to someone» is a formal phrase meaning to look after them.
fact: A minister is a person in charge of a government department, such as the minister for education.
fact: «In the UK you do not vote for the prime minister directly.»
fact: The cabinet is the top team of ministers, and the leader chooses who is in it.
fact: In some Christian churches, a minister is a leader who leads the services.
fact: The Taoiseach is Ireland's head of government, like a prime minister.
fact: In the USA, similar people are usually called secretaries.
exercise: «The cabinet is the top team of ministers; a minister is in charge of one area, like health or education.» What is a minister in this sentence? | *A person in charge of one area of government, like health or education | A pupil who is top of the class | A kind of church bell | A plan for taxes
exercise: Which job is a government leader? | Head teacher | Ice cream van driver | Football captain | *Prime minister
exercise: In church, what does a minister lead? | Football matches | Traffic on the road | *Services and worship | Tours of a museum
test: To minister to someone means what? | To forget them | To sing loudly to them | To ask them to leave | *To look after them
test: «A mini-budget» is a quick plan for what? | *Taxes | Cheap lunches | Church services | Shopping
exam: Does the UK prime minister get chosen by a direct public vote? | Prime ministers are picked by drawing names from a hat | Only children can vote for the prime minister | Yes, everyone votes for the prime minister on one day | *No, you do not vote for the prime minister directly
